    {
      "id": "C18",
      "query": "Bank supervisors' model-risk expectations stress conceptual soundness, ongoing monitoring, outcomes analysis and care when a model is used outside its original purpose. Apply that lens to a desk that wants to calibrate a rough-volatility model daily by replacing its slow Monte Carlo pricer with a fast polynomial surrogate built offline: what evidence does the research offer on accuracy, speed and build cost, and what controls and limitations would you insist on before production use?",
      "status": "partial",
      "answer": "This, however, still represents a reduction in building cost of 75%, 50% and 98%, with respect to [13], [14] and [2], respectively. [2012.07440v3.pdf p21]\n\nOnce these 10,000 values were obtained, it took the Rank Adaptive Algorithm under 5 minutes to obtain a TT-format Chebyshev Tensor — in Matlab. [2012.07440v3.pdf p18]\n\nIt took the Rank Adaptive Algorithm under 8 minutes to obtain a TT-format Chebyshev Tensor — in Matlab. [2012.07440v3.pdf p20]\n\nHowever, outside of it, there is no guarantee. [2012.07440v3.pdf p14]\n\nChebyshev Tensors do not extrapolate. [2012.07440v3.pdf p23]\n\nIn principle, the tensor built should work well for many weeks or monthts in the future. [2012.07440v3.pdf p18]\n\nPerhaps one should consider building a new one once market conditions change substantially. [2012.07440v3.pdf p18]\n\nThe choice of what tensor _X_ to try at each iteration is driven by the loss on the training set; the verification of whether the algorithm has converged is done using both training loss and testing loss. [2012.07440v3.pdf p12]\n\nThe greater the dimension, the less effective it is. [2012.07440v3.pdf p23]\n\nThe maximum dimension tested was 13. [2012.07440v3.pdf p23]\n\nWe do not know what will be the maximum dimension for which the presented technique would work. [2012.07440v3.pdf p23]\n\nWhen it is not, the pricing function is used. [2012.07440v3.pdf p15]\n\nTherefore, one is restricted to either optimisation routines that admit domain constraints — such as the ones considered in this paper — or calibrations that use a combination of Chebyshev Tensors and pricing model. [2012.07440v3.pdf p23]",
      "latency_seconds": 102.51109858299606,
      "returned_chunks": 49,
